{% set policy = row('org.peer-network.workload.benchmarks', name='structural-series') %}# Structural workload measurements · `rec:design:workload-benchmark-series`

**Convention (Workload inputs)** · `conv:harness:workload-benchmark-inputs` Component curves measure a declared deterministic recipe through public constructors and validators. Correctness is checked before sampling and after the timed series; input construction is excluded, while allocations made by the operation and destruction of its returned owned output remain timed. Consuming marker operations receive a fresh input clone outside each timed iteration. Fixture proof equality measures structural evidence handling, not cryptographic verification or chain finality. A refused, unsupported or incomplete point remains an explicitly typed result and cannot be fitted as successful throughput. Source, configuration, dimensions, limits, setup, raw samples and resource scope accompany every measurement. Resource samples describe the build container's cgroup, not other logins or the node as a whole; waited process accounting gives the campaign's own CPU. Load averages are recorded as context, without attributing their activity to other logins. Every float in the authored carrier uses exponent-free decimal notation, expanding exactly the digits of its shortest round-trip representation. The writer preserves the parsed value, including signed zero; the reader refuses other spellings. Every retained value parses back identically to the campaign raw result, as checked by the round-trip witness. The generated dataset carries those same values in the documents serializer's canonical form; its spelling need not match the authored input. The input rule prevents ambiguous digit runs without rounding evidence or changing the serializer. These curves declare no host workload, production API limit or capacity.

**Record (Sampling contract)** · `rec:workload:sampling` Full campaigns use {{ policy.number_forms.samples | display }} samples, {{ policy.number_forms.warmup_ms | display }} ms warm-up, {{ policy.number_forms.measurement_ms | display }} ms measurement targets and {{ policy.number_forms.resamples | display }} statistical resamples, with {{ policy.sampling }} iteration scheduling. The profile is {{ policy.profile }} and the deterministic seed is {{ policy.number_forms.seed | display }}. These are bounded sampling settings, not elapsed deadlines: a slow operation completes and retains its measured cost. A serialized pilot precedes a full series. The existing foundation smoke retains its settings; the extra smoke points are declared in the grid carrier. Full campaigns run serially at idle priority on a recorded allowed CPU with a separate build target. Timing is nonverdict under (`rule:devperf:nonverdict`). The dataset names each package-owned construction control. Result association is checked by (`claim:harness:workload-result-binding`).

